{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734762",
      "title": "Handling Side Effects with useEffect()",
      "sourceHash": "3dabbcf3f8d3e3ba8588bd7c79c7c9bf2d5b3fa168383c9d04f40a928baa9f52",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "So how can we fetch posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 6.873,
          "en": "when we first visit or reload this page?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "Well, for that, you could, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.51,
          "en": "say that you go to PostsList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.51,
          "end": 15.03,
          "en": "because that's where we need the posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.03,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "And we also send a fetch request here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 22.11,
          "en": "We target the same URL as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.11,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "because if we take a look at the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 25.83,
          "en": "we see that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 29.763,
          "en": "a get request to /posts gives us all our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.56,
          "end": 34.53,
          "en": "And then here, we already send a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.53,
          "end": 36.33,
          "en": "because as mentioned, that's the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.33,
          "end": 37.47,
          "en": "for the fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.47,
          "end": 39.816,
          "en": "so we don't need to configure this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.816,
          "end": 42.45,
          "en": "And now what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.45,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "Well, now in the end, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 47.67,
          "en": "that we update our posts here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.67,
          "end": 49.833,
          "en": "whenever we got a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 55.76,
          "en": "Well, for that, you could try to use async await like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 57.75,
          "en": "but this is not really supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.75,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "Your component functions must return JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "or some other values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "but promises should not be returned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 67.89,
          "en": "at least for this standard component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.89,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "without using any extra framework on top of React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 72.81,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.81,
          "end": 74.88,
          "en": "So promises may not be returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.88,
          "end": 77.61,
          "en": "and since adding async in front of a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.61,
          "end": 80.67,
          "en": "always ensures that this function returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "because any data returned by the function gets wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "into a promise, we must not use async here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 89.31,
          "en": "and we therefore can't use await here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 91.71000000000001,
          "en": "But of course, we could use the standard old school way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.71000000000001,
          "end": 93.47999999999999,
          "en": "of handling the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.47999999999999,
          "end": 95.49000000000001,
          "en": "and add the then method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.49000000000001,
          "end": 97.97999999999999,
          "en": "to get our response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.97999999999999,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "and then return response.json to unpack the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 103.22999999999999,
          "en": "from the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.22999999999999,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "because that's how you do it with this response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "There is a JSON method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "which then ultimately gives you the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 111.423,
          "en": "that was sent back from the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.5,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "And that data that's sent back is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 118.953,
          "en": "with a posts key that holds all the fetched posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.36,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "So we could add another then block here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 126.42,
          "en": "and then access data.posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.42,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "and there to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 131.04,
          "en": "we might want to call setPosts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.04,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "and set our posts to data.posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "But we should not do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 138.91,
          "en": "You should not save that, you should not write this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.8,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "because if you would write this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "it theoretically would update the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 150.29,
          "en": "with the new posts but it would cause an infinite loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 152.403,
          "en": "and why would it do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 157.5,
          "en": "Well, simply because whenever you update your state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.5,
          "end": 159.48,
          "en": "as you learned, your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 159.48,
          "end": 162.12,
          "en": "gets executed again by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 162.12,
          "end": 164.46,
          "en": "That's one of the key ideas of React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 164.46,
          "end": 167.18,
          "en": "that updating the state causes the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 167.18,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "to be executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 172.47,
          "en": "so that React can update the UI if needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 172.47,
          "end": 175.56,
          "en": "However, if this component function executes again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.56,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "this fetch request also gets sent again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 181.41,
          "en": "So we sent another request, we get data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 184.26,
          "en": "we update the state and the loop begins again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 184.26,
          "end": 187.44,
          "en": "So this is not code we wanna write like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 187.44,
          "end": 189.273,
          "en": "It would cause an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.04,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "So therefore, since that's not the solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 196.59,
          "en": "for fetching the posts, how should we do it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 196.59,
          "end": 198.75,
          "en": "Well, this is, of course, a common problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 200.7,
          "en": "and therefore, React has a solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 200.7,
          "end": 202.803,
          "en": "It has another hook we can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 207.39,
          "en": "Now, the hook we can use to solve problems like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 207.39,
          "end": 211.47,
          "en": "where we effectively wanna cause a side effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 211.47,
          "end": 212.94,
          "en": "in our component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 215.52,
          "en": "so where we wanna trigger some action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 215.52,
          "end": 218.7,
          "en": "that does not directly influence the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 221.07,
          "en": "but maybe indirectly in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 221.07,
          "end": 222.51,
          "en": "or that does anything else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.51,
          "end": 225.63,
          "en": "that's not related to rendering the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.63,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "In such cases, we get another hook we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 229.983,
          "en": "and that would be the useEffect hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 233.403,
          "en": "which is there to wrap side effects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 234.63,
          "end": 237.57,
          "en": "useEffect allows you to safely run code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 240.27,
          "en": "without causing an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 240.27,
          "end": 241.62,
          "en": "but how does it work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 241.62,
          "end": 244.5,
          "en": "Well, you execute useEffect like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 244.5,
          "end": 248.46,
          "en": "And unlike useState, it does then not return a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 248.46,
          "end": 250.98,
          "en": "Instead, it takes a function as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 250.98,
          "end": 253.473,
          "en": "and as a second argument, an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 254.43,
          "end": 257.553,
          "en": "So two arguments that must be passed to useEffect:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 257.553,
          "end": 259.533,
          "en": "a function and an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 260.73,
          "end": 262.95,
          "en": "Now, I'll come back to the array in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 262.95,
          "end": 264.873,
          "en": "Let's first focus on the function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 265.95,
          "end": 269.1,
          "en": "This function will be executed by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 269.1,
          "end": 273.03,
          "en": "for you whenever it considers this effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 273.03,
          "end": 275.43,
          "en": "to require execution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 275.43,
          "end": 278.97,
          "en": "and I'll get back to when it considers this effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 278.97,
          "end": 282.27,
          "en": "to require execution in just a couple of seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 282.27,
          "end": 284.82,
          "en": "but I can tell you that this second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 284.82,
          "end": 287.223,
          "en": "this array has something to do with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 288.51,
          "end": 290.58,
          "en": "We can, however, now grab our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 290.58,
          "end": 291.9,
          "en": "and put it in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 291.9,
          "end": 294.93,
          "en": "and we could now also actually wrap it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 297.23199999999997,
          "en": "into an extra function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 297.23199999999997,
          "end": 299.01,
          "en": "fetchPosts could be the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 299.01,
          "end": 300.27,
          "en": "which is an async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 300.27,
          "end": 302.86,
          "en": "which is defined inside of the effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 303.78,
          "end": 305.55,
          "en": "so that we can move our code in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 305.55,
          "end": 309.39300000000003,
          "en": "and actually use await to get our response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 310.38,
          "end": 314.61,
          "en": "And then also get our responseData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 314.61,
          "end": 316.74,
          "en": "by awaiting response.json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 316.74,
          "end": 318.96,
          "en": "so that we have this more readable code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 318.96,
          "end": 320.49,
          "en": "And then we update our posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 320.49,
          "end": 322.803,
          "en": "with the resData.posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 324.48,
          "end": 327.96,
          "en": "I created this extra function in this effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 327.96,
          "end": 330.48,
          "en": "instead of turning the effect function itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 330.48,
          "end": 331.86,
          "en": "into an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 331.86,
          "end": 334.08,
          "en": "because useEffect takes a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 334.08,
          "end": 336.65999999999997,
          "en": "that should not return a promise itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 336.65999999999997,
          "end": 338.73,
          "en": "but that instead should return nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 338.73,
          "end": 340.47,
          "en": "or a cleanup function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 340.47,
          "end": 342.39,
          "en": "which is not too important for us here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 342.39,
          "end": 345.24,
          "en": "which I do, of course, cover in my Complete Guide course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 345.24,
          "end": 347.28,
          "en": "but which we can ignore here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 349.59000000000003,
          "en": "But we should not return a promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 349.59000000000003,
          "end": 350.90999999999997,
          "en": "for this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 350.90999999999997,
          "end": 353.34000000000003,
          "en": "and therefore, we should not add async here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 353.34000000000003,
          "end": 355.83,
          "en": "Instead, I create an inner nested function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 355.83,
          "end": 358.86,
          "en": "which I then simply immediately execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 358.86,
          "end": 360.453,
          "en": "inside of this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 361.344,
          "end": 364.293,
          "en": "And this trick allows me to use async await in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 365.58,
          "end": 367.65,
          "en": "But back to the effect function itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 367.65,
          "end": 369.93,
          "en": "and the idea behind it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 369.93,
          "end": 372,
          "en": "As mentioned, React will now decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 372,
          "end": 374.07,
          "en": "when this function gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 374.07,
          "end": 378.15,
          "en": "and therefore, when this function gets executed indirectly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 378.15,
          "end": 381.48,
          "en": "And I can tell you that now with this setup here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 381.48,
          "end": 383.82,
          "en": "it will not always get executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 383.82,
          "end": 386.49,
          "en": "when this component function executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 386.49,
          "end": 388.35,
          "en": "Instead, if we save this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 388.35,
          "end": 390.21,
          "en": "and we reload the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 390.21,
          "end": 392.97,
          "en": "you see that now this post appears magically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 392.97,
          "end": 395.42,
          "en": "and that's, of course, the post from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 396.33,
          "end": 397.5,
          "en": "And there we can prove this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 397.5,
          "end": 399.03,
          "en": "If I go to the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 399.03,
          "end": 401.4,
          "en": "and I would edit the body here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 401.4,
          "end": 404.823,
          "en": "in posts.json, and save the updated file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 405.72,
          "end": 408.33,
          "en": "and I then go back to this app and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 408.33,
          "end": 411.3,
          "en": "you see that was uploaded here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 411.3,
          "end": 413.31,
          "en": "So this data is coming from the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 413.31,
          "end": 415.05,
          "en": "thanks to useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 415.05,
          "end": 417.06,
          "en": "But how exactly is this function working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 417.06,
          "end": 420.003,
          "en": "and why is it now not causing an infinite loop?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 421.17,
          "end": 423.63,
          "en": "This useEffect function here, this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 423.63,
          "end": 426.87,
          "en": "is now preventing an infinite loop from occurring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 426.87,
          "end": 428.31,
          "en": "by simply making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 428.31,
          "end": 431.43,
          "en": "that this effect function does not always execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 431.43,
          "end": 433.95,
          "en": "when the component function executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 433.95,
          "end": 435.81,
          "en": "It executes sometimes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 435.81,
          "end": 437.76,
          "en": "when the component function executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 437.76,
          "end": 440.31,
          "en": "Otherwise we wouldn't have fetched the posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 440.31,
          "end": 441.45,
          "en": "but not always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 441.45,
          "end": 443.7,
          "en": "But when does it execute?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 443.7,
          "end": 446.4,
          "en": "Well, that's controlled with this second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 446.4,
          "end": 449.763,
          "en": "that's passed to useEffect, this array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 450.63,
          "end": 454.5,
          "en": "This array in the end specifies the dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 454.5,
          "end": 456.48,
          "en": "of your effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 456.48,
          "end": 459.06,
          "en": "And a dependency is simply any variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 459.06,
          "end": 462.54,
          "en": "or function that might be defined outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 462.54,
          "end": 464.37,
          "en": "of this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 464.37,
          "end": 467.73,
          "en": "anywhere in your React components, in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 467.73,
          "end": 470.673,
          "en": "or some parent component passed down through props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 471.75,
          "end": 475.35,
          "en": "And whenever such a variable or function defined outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 475.35,
          "end": 477.21,
          "en": "of the effect function changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 477.21,
          "end": 479.73,
          "en": "receives a new value, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 479.73,
          "end": 482.193,
          "en": "this effect function will be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 483.15,
          "end": 484.77,
          "en": "Now, if we have an empty array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 484.77,
          "end": 488.13,
          "en": "it simply means this function has no dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 488.13,
          "end": 491.04,
          "en": "and therefore, it will never be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 491.04,
          "end": 493.32,
          "en": "Instead, React will only execute it once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 493.32,
          "end": 496.59,
          "en": "and that's when this component is first rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 496.59,
          "end": 498.72,
          "en": "And technically, it gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 498.72,
          "end": 500.85,
          "en": "after the component first rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 500.85,
          "end": 503.43,
          "en": "so theoretically, the component first renders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 503.43,
          "end": 504.6,
          "en": "without any posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 504.6,
          "end": 507.63,
          "en": "and then it immediately executes this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 507.63,
          "end": 509.493,
          "en": "where the posts get updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 510.42,
          "end": 511.98,
          "en": "But that's all so fast",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 511.98,
          "end": 514.62,
          "en": "that we only see the final state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 514.62,
          "end": 516.333,
          "en": "where the posts are fetched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 517.26,
          "end": 519.15,
          "en": "But that's how this executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 519.15,
          "end": 521.67,
          "en": "And this now gives us fine-grained control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 521.67,
          "end": 524.07,
          "en": "over when this executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 524.07,
          "end": 526.08,
          "en": "So that's how we can handle side effects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 526.08,
          "end": 528.33,
          "en": "like sending HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 528.33,
          "end": 529.95,
          "en": "Again, we, of course, dive deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 529.95,
          "end": 532.17,
          "en": "into effects and all these things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 532.17,
          "end": 533.46,
          "en": "in my Complete Guide course",
